<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mieszko III the Old</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1126–1202</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mieszko III the Old was a Piast duke of Greater <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, which he received under the testament of his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boleslaw-iii-wrymouth">Bolesław III Wrymouth</a> in 1138. He was also high duke of Poland, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krakow">Kraków</a> several times between 1173 and his death in 1202, but his harsh rule provoked revolts. The long struggle between his descendants and rival Piast lines shaped Greater Poland in the 13th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mieszko-iii-the-old.jpg" alt="Mieszko III the Old" width="320" height="396" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mieszko_III.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
